cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MANTA — Marine Amplicon Network Time-series Analysis"
message: "If you use MANTA in your work, please cite it, and cite the methods it calls."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Blumbach
    given-names: Ben
repository-code: "https://github.com/benblumbach-eng/manta"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  MANTA is a web platform for marine amplicon time series. Sequencing data run through a fixed
  analysis chain (DADA2, OTTER, Neo4j) and become searchable, visual and reproducible in a
  browser: a world map, co-occurrence and directed networks, Louvain modules, ASV detail pages,
  and an assistant that answers with typed tools which look values up in the graph. MANTA does
  not reimplement methods; it calls them and connects their results.
keywords:
  - amplicon sequencing
  - marine microbial ecology
  - time series
  - co-occurrence network
  - convergent cross mapping
  - Neo4j
  - DADA2
